RQ 6.2.1: Calibration Over Time
======================================================================

Loading data from: step02_calibration_scores.csv
  Rows: 400, Columns: ['UID', 'test', 'composite_ID', 'TSVR_hours', 'z_theta_accuracy', 'z_theta_confidence', 'calibration']
  Scaled TSVR_hours by 100 -> Time

Fitting LMM: calibration ~ Time
  Groups: UID
  Random effects: ~Time
  Model converged: True
  Log-likelihood: -503.61
  AIC: 1019.22

--- DIAGNOSTIC RESULTS ---

1. NORMALITY CHECK (QQ Plot + Shapiro-Wilk)
  Shapiro-Wilk (n=400): W=0.9770, p=0.000006
  Interpretation: FAIL - Significant non-normality (but LMM robust with N>100)

2. HOMOSCEDASTICITY CHECK (Residuals vs Fitted)
  Breusch-Pagan: χ²=12.1125, p=0.000501
  Interpretation: FAIL - Heteroscedasticity present (consider robust SE)

  Plots saved: rq_6_2_1_diagnostics.png

3. INFLUENTIAL OBSERVATIONS (Cook's D)
  Threshold: 4/n = 0.0100
  Max Cook's D: 0.0237
  Observations > threshold: 5 (1.2%)
  Interpretation: PASS - Few influential observations (<5%)

4. OVERALL ASSESSMENT
  Overall: REVIEW - Multiple issues: non-normality, heteroscedasticity
  Thesis impact: Document limitations; consider robust SE or alternative models

